IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap2-3val`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2015(d)(4): employment and training (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
-- JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- The paragraph addresses the State agency and the Secretary. Each duty is encoded as "the State agency is required to ...": JUST TRUE when its conditions hold, NOTHING otherwise.

§ `Section 2015(d)(4)(A): the program the State agency must implement`

-- src:596 | (A) In general.—
-- src:597 | (i) Implementation.—
-- src:598 | Each State agency shall implement an employment and training program designed by the State agency, in consultation with the State workforce development board, or, if the State demonstrates that consultation with private employers or employer organizations would be more effective or efficient, in consultation with private employers or employer organizations, and approved by the Secretary for the purpose of assisting members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will—
-- src:599 | (I) increase the ability of the household members to obtain regular employment; and
-- src:600 | (II) meet State or local workforce needs.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(A)(i) (src:596-600)
GIVEN `the program is designed by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency consulted the State workforce development board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State demonstrates that consultation with private employers or employer organizations would be more effective or efficient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency consulted private employers or employer organizations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has approved the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program is for assisting members of participating households in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase their ability to obtain regular employment and meet State or local workforce needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(A)(i) the State agency is required to implement the program` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to implement a program of the described design; "Each State agency shall implement an employment and training program designed by the State agency, in consultation with ..., and approved by the Secretary"
    IF `the program is designed by the State agency`
       AND (`the State agency consulted the State workforce development board`
            OR (`the State demonstrates that consultation with private employers or employer organizations would be more effective or efficient` AND `the State agency consulted private employers or employer organizations`))
       AND `the Secretary has approved the program`
       AND `the program is for assisting members of participating households in gaining skills, training, work, or experience that will increase their ability to obtain regular employment and meet State or local workforce needs`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:601 | (ii) Statewide workforce development system.—
-- src:602 | Each component of an employment and training program carried out under this paragraph and implemented to meet the purposes of clause (i) shall be delivered through a statewide workforce development system, unless the component is not available locally through such a system.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(A)(ii) (src:601-602)
GIVEN `the component is carried out under this paragraph and implemented to meet the purposes of clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the component is available locally through a statewide workforce development system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(A)(ii) the component must be delivered through the statewide workforce development system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Each component of an employment and training program carried out under this paragraph and implemented to meet the purposes of clause (i)"
        IF NOT `the component is carried out under this paragraph and implemented to meet the purposes of clause (i)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the component is not available locally through such a system"
        IF NOT `the component is available locally through a statewide workforce development system` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 2015(d)(4)(B): what an employment and training program and a workforce partnership are`

DECLARE `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) component` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(I) supervised job search programs`
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(II) job search training programs`
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(III) workfare programs operated under section 2029`
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(IV) work experience or training programs` HAS
        `it does not replace the employment of an individual not participating` IS A BOOLEAN
        `it provides the same benefits and working conditions as comparable work at the job site` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(V) educational programs or activities`
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VI) self-employment programs`
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VII) job retention programs` HAS `days of job retention services after the individual gains employment` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VIII) programs and activities under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(iv)` HAS `the Secretary determined they have the most demonstrable impact` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(IX) other programs approved by the Secretary or the State` HAS `approved by the Secretary or the State under regulations issued by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:606 | The term “employment and training program” means a program that contains case management services such as comprehensive intake assessments, individualized service plans, progress monitoring, or coordination with service providers and one or more of the following components, except that the State agency shall retain the option to apply employment requirements prescribed under this clause to a program applicant at the time of application:
-- src:607 | (I) Supervised job search programs that occur at State-approved locations at which the activities of participants shall be directly supervised and the timing and activities of participants tracked in accordance with guidelines issued by the State.
-- src:608 | (II) Job search training programs that include, to the extent determined appropriate by the State agency, reasonable job search training and support activities that may consist of employability assessments, training in techniques to increase employability, job placement services, or other direct training or support activities, including educational programs, determined by the State agency to expand the job search abilities or employability of those subject to the program.
-- src:609 | (III) Workfare programs operated under section 2029 of this title.
-- src:610 | (IV) Programs designed to improve the employability of household members through actual work experience or training, or both, and to enable individuals employed or trained under such programs to move promptly into regular public or private employment, including subsidized employment and apprenticeships. An employment or training experience program established under this clause shall—
-- src:611 | (aa) not provide any work that has the effect of replacing the employment of an individual not participating in the employment or training experience program; and
-- src:612 | (bb) provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site to employees performing comparable work for comparable hours.
-- src:613 | (V) Educational programs or activities to improve basic skills and literacy, or otherwise improve employability, including educational programs determined by the State agency to expand the job search abilities or employability of those subject to the program under this paragraph.
-- src:614 | (VI) Programs designed to increase the self-sufficiency of recipients through self-employment, including programs that provide instruction for self-employment ventures.
-- src:615 | (VII) Programs intended to ensure job retention by providing job retention services, if the job retention services are provided for a period of not less than 30 days but not more than 90 days after an individual who received employment and training services under this paragraph gains employment.
-- src:616 | (VIII) Programs and activities under clause (iv) of section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title that the Secretary determines, based on results from the independent evaluations conducted under clause (vii)(I) of such section, have the most demonstrable impact on the ability of participants to find and retain employment that leads to increased household income and reduced reliance on public assistance.
-- src:617 | (IX) As approved by the Secretary or the State under regulations issued by the Secretary, other employment, educational and training programs, projects, and experiments, such as a supported work program, aimed at accomplishing the purpose of the employment and training program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) (src:606-617)
GIVEN c IS A `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) component`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) the component is one of those the definition lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(I) supervised job search programs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(II) job search training programs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(III) workfare programs operated under section 2029` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall— (aa) not provide any work that has the effect of replacing the employment of an individual not participating ...; and (bb) provide the same benefits and working conditions"
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(IV) work experience or training programs` a b THEN JUST (a AND b)
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(V) educational programs or activities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VI) self-employment programs` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not less than 30 days but not more than 90 days after an individual ... gains employment"
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VII) job retention programs` n THEN JUST (n AT LEAST 30 AND n AT MOST 90)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "that the Secretary determines ... have the most demonstrable impact"; with no determination supplied the answer is NOTHING
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(VIII) programs and activities under section 2025(h)(1)(F)(iv)` d THEN d
    WHEN `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i)(IX) other programs approved by the Secretary or the State` ok THEN JUST ok

-- src:605 | (i) Employment and training program.—
-- src:606 | The term “employment and training program” means a program that contains case management services such as comprehensive intake assessments, individualized service plans, progress monitoring, or coordination with service providers and one or more of the following components, except that the State agency shall retain the option to apply employment requirements prescribed under this clause to a program applicant at the time of application:
-- src:607 | (I) Supervised job search programs that occur at State-approved locations at which the activities of participants shall be directly supervised and the timing and activities of participants tracked in accordance with guidelines issued by the State.
-- src:608 | (II) Job search training programs that include, to the extent determined appropriate by the State agency, reasonable job search training and support activities that may consist of employability assessments, training in techniques to increase employability, job placement services, or other direct training or support activities, including educational programs, determined by the State agency to expand the job search abilities or employability of those subject to the program.
-- src:609 | (III) Workfare programs operated under section 2029 of this title.
-- src:610 | (IV) Programs designed to improve the employability of household members through actual work experience or training, or both, and to enable individuals employed or trained under such programs to move promptly into regular public or private employment, including subsidized employment and apprenticeships. An employment or training experience program established under this clause shall—
-- src:611 | (aa) not provide any work that has the effect of replacing the employment of an individual not participating in the employment or training experience program; and
-- src:612 | (bb) provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site to employees performing comparable work for comparable hours.
-- src:613 | (V) Educational programs or activities to improve basic skills and literacy, or otherwise improve employability, including educational programs determined by the State agency to expand the job search abilities or employability of those subject to the program under this paragraph.
-- src:614 | (VI) Programs designed to increase the self-sufficiency of recipients through self-employment, including programs that provide instruction for self-employment ventures.
-- src:615 | (VII) Programs intended to ensure job retention by providing job retention services, if the job retention services are provided for a period of not less than 30 days but not more than 90 days after an individual who received employment and training services under this paragraph gains employment.
-- src:616 | (VIII) Programs and activities under clause (iv) of section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title that the Secretary determines, based on results from the independent evaluations conducted under clause (vii)(I) of such section, have the most demonstrable impact on the ability of participants to find and retain employment that leads to increased household income and reduced reliance on public assistance.
-- src:617 | (IX) As approved by the Secretary or the State under regulations issued by the Secretary, other employment, educational and training programs, projects, and experiments, such as a supported work program, aimed at accomplishing the purpose of the employment and training program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) (src:605-617)
GIVEN `the program contains case management services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the components the program contains` IS A LIST OF `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) component`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) the program is an employment and training program` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a program that contains case management services ... and one or more of the following components"
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the program contains case management services` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds` (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) the component is one of those the definition lists` c) `the components the program contains`)

-- src:606 | The term “employment and training program” means a program that contains case management services such as comprehensive intake assessments, individualized service plans, progress monitoring, or coordination with service providers and one or more of the following components, except that the State agency shall retain the option to apply employment requirements prescribed under this clause to a program applicant at the time of application:
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) (src:606-606)
GIVEN `the person is a program applicant at the time of application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(B)(i) the State agency may apply employment requirements under the clause to the applicant` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the State agency shall retain the option to apply employment requirements prescribed under this clause to a program applicant at the time of application"
    IF `the person is a program applicant at the time of application` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(ii) program` HAS
    `the program is operated by a private employer, an organization representing private employers, or a nonprofit organization providing services relating to workforce development` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the program is operated by an entity identified as an eligible provider of training services under section 122(d) of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary certifies, or the State agency certifies to the Secretary, the matters in items (AA) to (FF)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would assist participants who are members of participating households in gaining high-quality, work-relevant skills, training, work, or experience that will increase their ability to obtain regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours per week of training, work, or experience it would provide participants` IS A NUMBER
    `it would not use any funds authorized to be appropriated by this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would provide sufficient information, on request by the State agency, to show that participants are fulfilling any applicable work requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it would be willing to serve as a reference for participants for future employment or work-related programs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it meets any other criteria established by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 applies to the program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the program is in compliance with the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the program is a multistate program` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:619 | (I) In general.—
-- src:620 | The term “workforce partnership” means a program that—
-- src:621 | (aa) is operated by—
-- src:622 | (AA) a private employer, an organization representing private employers, or a nonprofit organization providing services relating to workforce development; or
-- src:623 | (BB) an entity identified as an eligible provider of training services under section 122(d) of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act (29 U.S.C. 3152(d));
-- src:624 | (bb) the Secretary certifies, or the State agency certifies to the Secretary—
-- src:625 | (AA) subject to subparagraph (N)(ii), would assist participants who are members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program in gaining high-quality, work-relevant skills, training, work, or experience that will increase the ability of the participants to obtain regular employment;
-- src:626 | (BB) subject to subparagraph (N)(ii), would provide participants with not less than 20 hours per week of training, work, or experience under subitem (AA);
-- src:627 | (CC) would not use any funds authorized to be appropriated by this chapter;
-- src:628 | (DD) would provide sufficient information, on request by the State agency, for the State agency to determine that participants who are members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program are fulfilling any applicable work requirement under this subsection or subsection (o);
-- src:629 | (EE) would be willing to serve as a reference for participants who are members of households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for future employment or work-related programs; and
-- src:630 | (FF) meets any other criteria established by the Secretary, on the condition that the Secretary shall not establish any additional criteria that would impose significant paperwork burdens on the workforce partnership; and
-- src:631 | (cc) is in compliance with the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 (29 U.S.C. 201 et seq.), if applicable.
-- src:632 | (II) Inclusion.—
-- src:633 | The term “workforce partnership” includes a multistate program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(B)(ii) (src:619-633)
GIVEN p IS A `s 2015(d)(4)(B)(ii) program`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(B)(ii) the program is a workforce partnership` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “workforce partnership” means a program that— (aa) ...; (bb) ...; and (cc) ..."
    -- (II) "The term “workforce partnership” includes a multistate program": a multistate program is not excluded and must meet the same limbs
    JUST (   (p's `the program is operated by a private employer, an organization representing private employers, or a nonprofit organization providing services relating to workforce development`
              OR p's `the program is operated by an entity identified as an eligible provider of training services under section 122(d) of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`)
         AND p's `the Secretary certifies, or the State agency certifies to the Secretary, the matters in items (AA) to (FF)`
         AND p's `it would assist participants who are members of participating households in gaining high-quality, work-relevant skills, training, work, or experience that will increase their ability to obtain regular employment`
         AND p's `hours per week of training, work, or experience it would provide participants` AT LEAST 20
         AND p's `it would not use any funds authorized to be appropriated by this chapter`
         AND p's `it would provide sufficient information, on request by the State agency, to show that participants are fulfilling any applicable work requirement`
         AND p's `it would be willing to serve as a reference for participants for future employment or work-related programs`
         AND p's `it meets any other criteria established by the Secretary`
         AND ((NOT p's `the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 applies to the program`) OR p's `the program is in compliance with the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938`))

§ `Section 2015(d)(4)(C) to (H): the State agency's options and limits`

-- src:634 | (C) The State agency may provide that participation in an employment and training program may supplement or supplant other employment-related requirements imposed on those subject to the program.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(C) (src:634-634)
GIVEN `the other requirements are employment-related requirements imposed on those subject to the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(C) the State agency may provide that participation supplements or supplants the other requirements` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other employment-related requirements imposed on those subject to the program"
    IF `the other requirements are employment-related requirements imposed on those subject to the program` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:635 | (D)
-- src:636 | (i) Each State agency may exempt from any requirement for participation in any program under this paragraph categories of household members.
-- src:637 | (ii) Each State agency may exempt from any requirement for participation individual household members not included in any category designated as exempt under clause (i).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(D)(i) and (ii) (src:635-637)
GIVEN `the exemption is for a category of household members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household member is in a category designated as exempt under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(D) the State agency may exempt the category or the individual member from the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- clause (i): "may exempt from any requirement for participation in any program under this paragraph categories of household members"
        IF `the exemption is for a category of household members` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- clause (ii): "individual household members not included in any category designated as exempt under clause (i)"
        IF NOT `the household member is in a category designated as exempt under clause (i)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a member already in an exempt category needs no individual exemption
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:638 | (iii) Any exemption of a category or individual under this subparagraph shall be periodically evaluated to determine whether the exemption continues to be valid.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(D)(iii) (src:638-638)
GIVEN `the exemption was made under subparagraph (D)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(D)(iii) the exemption is to be periodically evaluated to determine whether it continues to be valid` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any exemption of a category or individual under this subparagraph"
    IF `the exemption was made under subparagraph (D)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:639 | (E) Requirements for participation for certain individuals.—
-- src:640 | (i) In general.—
-- src:641 | Each State agency shall establish requirements for participation by individuals not exempt under subparagraph (D) in one or more employment and training programs under this paragraph, including the extent to which any individual is required to participate.
-- src:642 | (ii) Variation.—
-- src:643 | The requirements under clause (i) may vary among participants.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(E)(i) and (ii) (src:639-643)
GIVEN `the individual is exempt under subparagraph (D)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(E) the State agency is required to establish requirements for participation by the individual` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "individuals not exempt under subparagraph (D)"; the requirements "may vary among participants"
    IF `the individual is exempt under subparagraph (D)` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:644 | (iii) Application to workforce partnerships.—
-- src:645 | To the extent that a State agency requires an individual to participate in an employment and training program, the State agency shall consider an individual participating in a workforce partnership to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii) (src:644-645)
GIVEN `the State agency requires the individual to participate in an employment and training program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual participates in a workforce partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(E)(iii) the individual is considered to be in compliance with the employment and training requirements` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the extent that a State agency requires an individual to participate in an employment and training program"
    IF `the State agency requires the individual to participate in an employment and training program` AND `the individual participates in a workforce partnership` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:647 | (i) The total hours of work in an employment and training program carried out under this paragraph required of members of a household, together with the hours of work of such members in any program carried out under section 2029 of this title, in any month collectively may not exceed a number of hours equal to the household’s allotment for such month divided by the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 [29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)].
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(F)(i) (src:647-647)
GIVEN `the total hours of work required of the household's members in an employment and training program and in any program under section 2029 in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the household's allotment for the month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual is voluntarily electing to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(F)(i) the required hours of the household's members exceed the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be subject to the limitations described in clauses (i) and (ii)" (clause (iii), voluntary election)
        IF `the individual is voluntarily electing to participate` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the limit is "a number of hours equal to the household’s allotment for such month divided by the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or Federal minimum hourly rate"
        IF `the total hours of work required of the household's members in an employment and training program and in any program under section 2029 in the month` GREATER THAN `the household's allotment for the month, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate, in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any month collectively may not exceed a number of hours equal to the household’s allotment"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:648 | (ii) The total hours of participation in such program required of any member of a household, individually, in any month, together with any hours worked in another program carried out under section 2029 of this title and any hours worked for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity, shall not exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii) (src:648-648)
GIVEN `the hours of participation required of the member in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours worked in another program under section 2029` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours worked for compensation in cash or in kind in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the member is voluntarily electing to participate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(F)(ii) the required hours of the member exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be subject to the limitations described in clauses (i) and (ii)" (clause (iii), voluntary election)
        IF `the member is voluntarily electing to participate` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the hours of participation required of the member in the month` PLUS `the hours worked in another program under section 2029` PLUS `the hours worked for compensation in cash or in kind in any other capacity` GREATER THAN 120 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed one hundred and twenty hours per month"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:650 | (G) The State agency may operate any program component under this paragraph in which individuals elect to participate.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(G) (src:650-650)
GIVEN `individuals elect to participate in the program component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(G) the State agency may operate the program component` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any program component under this paragraph in which individuals elect to participate"
    IF `individuals elect to participate in the program component` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:651 | (H) Federal funds made available to a State agency for purposes of the component authorized under subparagraph (B)(i)(V) shall not be used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing services and activities that promote the purposes of this component.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(H) (src:651-651)
GIVEN `the funds were made available for the component under subparagraph (B)(i)(V)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they would be used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing services and activities that promote the purposes of the component` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(H) the Federal funds may be used` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing services and activities that promote the purposes of this component"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): funds for another component, or use that does not supplant
    IF `the funds were made available for the component under subparagraph (B)(i)(V)` AND `they would be used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing services and activities that promote the purposes of the component` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2015(d)(4)(I) to (M): costs, guidelines, funding and facilities`

-- src:653 | (i) The State agency shall provide payments or reimbursements to participants in programs carried out under this paragraph, including individuals participating under subparagraph (G), for—
-- src:654 | (I) the actual costs of transportation and other actual costs (other than dependent care costs), that are reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program; and
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I) (src:653-654)
GIVEN `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is an actual cost of transportation or another actual cost other than dependent care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(I) the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the cost` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the actual costs of transportation and other actual costs (other than dependent care costs), that are reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program"
    IF `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)`
       AND `the cost is an actual cost of transportation or another actual cost other than dependent care`
       AND `the cost is reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program`
        THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:655 | (II) the actual costs of such dependent care expenses that are determined by the State agency to be necessary for the participation of an individual in the program (other than an individual who is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV of such Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] is in operation), except that no such payment or reimbursement shall exceed the applicable local market rate. Individuals subject to the program under this paragraph may not be required to participate if dependent costs exceed the limit established by the State agency under this subclause or other actual costs exceed any limit established under subclause (I).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) (src:655-655)
GIVEN `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is an actual dependent care expense the State agency determined to be necessary for the participation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) the State agency is required to pay or reimburse the dependent care cost` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than an individual who is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act ...)"
        IF `the person is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV is in operation` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the actual costs of such dependent care expenses that are determined by the State agency to be necessary for the participation of an individual in the program"
        IF `the person is a participant in a program carried out under this paragraph, including an individual participating under subparagraph (G)` AND `the cost is an actual dependent care expense the State agency determined to be necessary for the participation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:655 | (II) the actual costs of such dependent care expenses that are determined by the State agency to be necessary for the participation of an individual in the program (other than an individual who is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV of such Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] is in operation), except that no such payment or reimbursement shall exceed the applicable local market rate. Individuals subject to the program under this paragraph may not be required to participate if dependent costs exceed the limit established by the State agency under this subclause or other actual costs exceed any limit established under subclause (I).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) (src:655-655)
GIVEN `the actual dependent care cost, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable local market rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) the most the State agency may pay or reimburse for the dependent care, in dollars` MEANS
    -- "except that no such payment or reimbursement shall exceed the applicable local market rate"
    `s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` `the actual dependent care cost, in dollars` `the applicable local market rate, in dollars`

-- src:655 | (II) the actual costs of such dependent care expenses that are determined by the State agency to be necessary for the participation of an individual in the program (other than an individual who is the caretaker relative of a dependent in a family receiving benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) in a local area where an employment, training, or education program under title IV of such Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] is in operation), except that no such payment or reimbursement shall exceed the applicable local market rate. Individuals subject to the program under this paragraph may not be required to participate if dependent costs exceed the limit established by the State agency under this subclause or other actual costs exceed any limit established under subclause (I).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(I)(i)(II) (src:655-655)
GIVEN `the dependent care costs exceed the limit the State agency established under subclause (II)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other actual costs exceed a limit established under subclause (I)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(I)(i) the individual may be required to participate in the program` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Individuals subject to the program under this paragraph may not be required to participate if dependent costs exceed the limit"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): costs within the limits
    IF `the dependent care costs exceed the limit the State agency established under subclause (II)` OR `other actual costs exceed a limit established under subclause (I)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:656 | (ii) In lieu of providing reimbursements or payments for dependent care expenses under clause (i), a State agency may, at its option, arrange for dependent care through providers by the use of purchase of service contracts or vouchers or by providing vouchers to the household.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii) (src:656-656)
