GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(I)(ii) the State agency may arrange dependent care instead of reimbursing it` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at its option, arrange for dependent care through providers by the use of purchase of service contracts or vouchers or by providing vouchers to the household"
    IF `the State agency arranges dependent care through providers by purchase of service contracts or vouchers, or provides vouchers to the household, in lieu of payments or reimbursements` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:657 | (iii) The value of any dependent care services provided for or arranged under clause (ii), or any amount received as a payment or reimbursement under clause (i), shall—
-- src:658 | (I) not be treated as income for the purposes of any other Federal or federally assisted program that bases eligibility for, or the amount of benefits on, need; and
