-- src:661 | (K) Limitation on funding.—
-- src:662 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this paragraph, the amount of funds a State agency uses to carry out this paragraph (including funds used to carry out subparagraph (I)) for participants who are receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) shall not exceed the amount of funds the State agency used in fiscal year 1995 to carry out this paragraph for participants who were receiving benefits in fiscal year 1995 under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(4)(K) (src:661-662)
GIVEN `the funds are used for participants who are receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the funds used in fiscal year 1995 for participants receiving benefits that year under a State program funded under part A of title IV, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(d)(4)(K) the funds the State agency uses exceed the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the funds are used for participants who are receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the funds used in fiscal year 1995 for participants receiving benefits that year under a State program funded under part A of title IV, in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed the amount of funds the State agency used in fiscal year 1995"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

